{{- /* What kind of machine is this — as a set, not a single label.

       A laptop is `host personal linux`; a devcontainer for a TypeScript web
       app is `container typescript web linux`. Anything that must not be
       installed or applied everywhere gates on one member of the set:

         {{ if contains " host " (includeTemplate "profiles" .) }}

       Three sources, and which is which is the whole design:

         detected     host/container, and the OS. A machine can work these out
                      about itself, so it is never asked.
         asked once   personal or work. Nothing can detect this, so
                      .chezmoi.toml.tmpl prompts on the first interactive init
                      and remembers the answer. Unasked means personal, which
                      is what CI, `mise run verify` and `devpod up` get.
         environment  the project's own profiles, from DOTFILES_PROFILES, set
                      by a devcontainer.json. They belong to the checkout
                      rather than to the machine.

       Assembled on every apply and never stored, so it cannot go stale: a
       project edits DOTFILES_PROFILES and the next apply reflects it.

       Padded with a space at each end, so a caller writes `contains " host "`
       and a profile named `ghost` cannot answer for `host`. A gate that
       silently matches the wrong machine is worse than one that never matches.

       The container half comes from .chezmoitemplates/is-container, shared with
       .chezmoiignore and the host-packages script, so the gates cannot drift
       apart. */ -}}
{{- $profiles := list -}}
{{- if eq (includeTemplate "is-container" .) "true" -}}
{{-   $profiles = append $profiles "container" -}}
{{- else -}}
{{-   $profiles = append $profiles "host" -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $profiles = append $profiles .chezmoi.os -}}
{{- $role := "personal" -}}
{{- if and (hasKey . "role") .role -}}
{{-   $role = .role -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $profiles = append $profiles $role -}}
{{- range splitList "," (env "DOTFILES_PROFILES") -}}
{{-   $p := trim . -}}
{{-   if $p -}}
{{-     $profiles = append $profiles $p -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- printf " %s " (join " " $profiles) -}}
